+# Walking history — 25 September 2026
+
+The existing Rule 30 history study gains `follow:walk` only in this map. CharacterBody3D roots in `em_walker` or `player_body` select a recorded row by local z. The selection changes only the three gold witnesses and the readout. It does not change the history, colours, collision, update clock or seed.
+
+The floor witness is widened from 6.1 to 8.8 m to reach the independent museum margin. Its line supplies no collision. A ground inscription introduces walking; the six existing controls remain. The selected row stays on departure. The desk lies outside the selection region, so its ROW control remains manual. Beyond the most recent row there is no invented continuation. RUN may keep appending rows while the visitor reads an earlier one.
+
+## Native verification
+
+37 checks pass. Seven real desktop mouse-ray events exercise the six controls. A supplied museum body walks to rows 0, 3, 10 and back to 5; every witness agrees while all stored rows, colours, visible instance positions and support flags remain equal to the arrival snapshot. Unrecorded space and out-of-bay/above-display bodies are ignored. A supplied player_body fixture exercises the XR group convention, not a tracked headset. The original 24-row limit, replay, seed/one-bit edits and unconfigured study remain intact.
+
+All five authored artifacts and their placements remain. The actual native museum screenshots and exact diff are in `doc/book/iterations/2026-09-25-ca-walking-history/index.html`. Full native log and source snapshots are retained. The final process exits 0 without GDScript errors; existing UID, environment, registry, renderer and generated-art material/build warnings remain. This pass does not measure Quest performance, whole-gallery traversal, tracked-hand reach, headset comfort or learner acceptance. A generated tiled pattern is not certified as a continuous traversable crossing.
+
+## Writing decision
+
+Keep the mature chapter. Add the walk and its reversal as an encounter with a retained past, followed by the distinction between a marker crossing a gap and a foot needing support. Preserve both code excerpts, all original arguments and the secondary collection. The historical map ID stays; its title remains “A history you can inhabit.” The actual Conway Life encounter is next, in CA_BeyondBinary. The rear Turing lab remains a secondary encounter requiring separate review.
